<title>INDIA: Indian rupee eases vs dlr on RBI's dollar purchase.</title>
<headline>Indian rupee eases vs dlr on RBI's dollar purchase.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Indian rupee eased to 35.79/80 after the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) intervened in the market on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said RBI bought dollars at 35.79, lifting the dollar to 35.792/802 in latest transactions from 35.76/77 opening.</p>
<p>The rupee would have tested the 35.75 mark if the RBI had not intervened, dealers said.</p>
<p>The forward dollar market was steady and uneventful, they said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
